/* book exam traps: Coil rating is not contact rating. A 24 V coil may switch 230 V mains, so give both when asked for a relay's ratings. | At standstill a DC motor has Eb = 0, so Ia = V ÷ Ra. A 12 V motor with 1 Ω that draws 2 A at load draws 12 A at start; the supply and driver must survive that. | Hold current is not pull-in current. Holding needs less current, and running a 10% duty-cycle coil at pull-in current continuously burns it out. */
